VALUES('BScN','Paper I','Medical-Surgical Nursing','Professional Practice','What does the term "therapeutic communication" refer to in nursing practice?','Using medical jargon to communicate with patients','Promoting open and honest communication with patients for therapeutic purposes','Providing written instructions to patients','Documenting patient information in the medical record','B','Therapeutic communication techniques: active listening, open-ended questions, reflection, silence, empathy, clarification. BScN nurses apply communication theory (Peplau''s interpersonal relations model) in complex patient interactions and teach communication skills to junior staff (Brunner & Suddarth; Peplau).','easy',NULL,'approved',NULL)ON CONFLICT(stem,cadre)DO NOTHING;

