VALUES('KRCHN','Paper I','Medical-Surgical Nursing','Patient Safety','What is the primary purpose of the nurse''s role in fall prevention?','To avoid providing assistance to at-risk patients','To document all patient falls','To prevent patient falls and minimise the risk of injury','To restrict patients to their beds','C','Nurses implement fall prevention strategies — risk assessment, bed alarms, non-slip footwear, call bell within reach, adequate lighting — to prevent falls and injury, a key patient safety indicator (Brunner & Suddarth; Kenya patient safety guidelines).','easy',NULL,'approved',NULL)ON CONFLICT(stem,cadre)DO NOTHING;

