VALUES('KRCHN','Paper I','Pharmacology','Endocrine Pharmacology','What is the primary goal of administering insulin therapy in nursing practice?','To promote high blood sugar levels','To decrease patient compliance','To maintain blood glucose levels within a target range','To minimise communication with the patient','C','Insulin therapy is administered to maintain blood glucose levels within a therapeutic target range in patients with diabetes mellitus, preventing hyperglycaemia and its complications (BNF; Kenya MOH diabetes management guidelines).','easy',NULL,'approved',NULL)ON CONFLICT(stem,cadre)DO NOTHING;

